A||||3||william_thorniii||Tach Filter and Temp Guage?||||5||
Z||000000||william_thorniii||02-26-2001||08:40 PM||||Friends,<P>My car (1987 DIS Duke - TH125) did two abnormal things the other day.  I was wondering if anyone else thought they may be related.  One night last week (while shamefully waiting in a drive-thru line), my tach began bouncing around and more importantly, my temp gauge shot up.  I have owned this car for over 50K miles and neither of these symptoms (either together or apart) have occured previously.  Furthermore, neither has happened since (have driven around 600 miles since then).<P>I assume the tach problem to be related to the tach filter and will work on replacing that right away... oh Rodney.  Was it pure coincidence that my temp gauge went screwy at the exact same time, or are they related in some way.  The engine was not overheating, merely the gauge was reading incorrectly... no worries there, although I did turn the A/C on to get the fan to kick in and ran around the back of my car to make sure that the decklid and engine vents were not too hot... no I am not paranoid ;~)<P>Any Suggestions,<P>Willilam T. Thorn, III||||reg||5
Z||000001||FieroJoe||02-26-2001||08:48 PM||||Though in the actual gauge cluster, I dont think the gauges are linked in anyway, except possibly grounds, I do remember reading recently a bad tach filter can screw up more than just the tach.  I believe that the temp gauge is engine grounded, and if the tach filter is screwing up things with the ground, maybe its making your temp gauge go screwy.<P>Either way, the main point is hopefully its just the tach filter screwing up more things that just the tach, and not a coolant problem.  Horses, not zebras!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>AIM: Snowboarder0311<BR>87 Coupe 5sp. - big resto in progress<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Rodney||02-27-2001||10:04 AM||||The 87-88 Tech 4 does not have a tach filter. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||william_thorniii||02-27-2001||11:31 AM||||Rodney,<P>THX for the information.  <P>Everyone,<P>Any other suggestions/ideas?<P>THX,<P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||5
